ives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 1-6\\cdot 8}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390719 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390719 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390719 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390719 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390719 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390719 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390719 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390719 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186390724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390719 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "94a86967-5a41-5f2d-8c19-38b625daba3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390720 #edb/ref 1080 "x=-\\frac{1}{50}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390720 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390720 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "af53f340-3e36-5545-937e-11e307962671" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390721 #edb/ref 1080 "x=-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390721 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390721 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f3ec4ea9-2509-5c2c-a216-2db5287d79fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390722 #edb/ref 1080 "x=\\frac{1}{50}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390722 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390722 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "99392c81-e8f0-5fb5-ae4c-99f2a069feb9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390723 #edb/ref 1080 "x=\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390723 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390723 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bff6331c-295a-540c-a6d8-28d96895301d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390724 #edb/ref 1080 "x=-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390724 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390724 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4d16e9a1-1407-53d0-b940-8956dc7a7aa2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391617 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391617 #edb/ref 1069 "q-33584" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391617 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391617 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=2t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+t\\,k$ at the point $P(2,1,1)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391617 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "93a1c03f-77b3-5fa3-b1a1-22418386cc31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391617 #edb/ref 1074 "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,j+y(t)\\,j+z(t)\\,k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by \n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(2,1,1)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k \\\\ 2t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+t\\,k & =2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2t=2 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ t=1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=1.$ This value satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(2,1,1)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2t\\,j+\\,k \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =2\\,i+2(1)\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(2,1,1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2\\,i+2\\,j+\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{2}{3}\\,j+\\frac{1}{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391618 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391618 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391618 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391618 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391618 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391618 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391618 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391618 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186391620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391618 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3d43ad92-b445-5432-aa1f-111fa6dcfbd4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391619 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,i+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,k" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391619 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391619 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9f60c71f-f1a0-5dc9-bc85-bc53e3b5d9e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391620 #edb/ref 1080 "\