ystem of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=2 \\\\ 3x+9y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392481 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "653d2739-ff74-51ff-bc93-114e79b1a15b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392481 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+3y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2-3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392482 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392482 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392482 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392482 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392482 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392482 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392482 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392482 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186392485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392482 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8ff50c54-cba8-5cc5-a898-6fa889298459" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392483 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392483 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392483 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "656236ac-76c2-57ac-afcc-6fef3eee767b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392484 #edb/ref 1080 "No solution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392484 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392484 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "21fc8fc7-0be2-53a6-99c7-2cb1e090034f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392485 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392485 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392485 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cb7cc337-7043-5f29-9a9e-c853229ab133" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392486 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392486 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392486 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4cc5f9be-53a1-53b5-83eb-dd3ed1177b70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392487 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392487 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392487 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a3cdc156-a512-50b5-bb71-be50d05948f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393215 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393215 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72726" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393215 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393215 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=4 \\\\ x=-2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393215 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cf30e2dd-fc54-551b-b230-ad61e11fe0db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393215 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=4 \\\\ x+2y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393216 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393217 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393216 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393218 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393216 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393216 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393216 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393216 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb